From: bearinmindcat <bearinmindcat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] enable -fwrapv in Clang for non-UBSan builds

Vanadium hardening: defined signed-integer-overflow (-fwrapv). Re-placed for
Chromium 150 (config("compiler"), after the arm64 stack-clash block; the
original v99 location drifted into config("linker") where cflags is undefined).
---
--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -473,6 +473,10 @@
     if (current_cpu == "arm64") {
       cflags += [ "-fstack-clash-protection" ]
     }
+
+    if (is_clang && !is_ubsan && !is_ubsan_security) {
+      cflags += [ "-fwrapv" ]
+    }
   }
 
   # Non-Apple Posix and Fuchsia compiler flags setup.
